==Battleground==
*3 [[Gabriel]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 8~10 seconds<sup>240f~300f</sup>.
*3 [[Metal Hippoe]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 80~86.67 seconds<sup>2,400f~2,600f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Sir Metal Seal]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Gabriel]]s spawn, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Metal Doge]]s spawn, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.
**2 [[Heavenly Hippoe]]s spawn, delay 48~53.33 seconds<sup>1,440f~1,600f</sup>.
**1 [[Super Metal Hippoe]] spawns.

==Strategy==
Most of the enemies are [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] so bring as many [[:Category:Critical Hit Cats|Critical Hitters]], [[:Category:Anti-Metal Cats|anti-Metal]] debuffers, and Critical Up [[Cat Combo|Combos]] as possible. Some obvious choices for Critical units include [[Jurassic Cat (Rare Cat)|Jurassic Cat Sitter]], [[Space Cat (Rare Cat)|Major Space Cat]], [[Catornado (Super Rare Cat)|Hurricat]], [[Crazed Moneko (Special Cat)|Corrupted Moneko]] and [[Cheerleader Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Waitress Cat]]. [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] can help, but is optional. Start off the level by stalling the Gabriels, and build up some money ([[Worker Cat]] Level 3-4). After you have sufficient funds, start spamming everything (other than non-Crit Combo units). Eventually, you should win.

==Trivia==
*Ticket Hunter G may be a reference to the game ''[[wikia:monsterhunter:Monster Hunter G|Monster Hunter G]]''; the stage within being called Monster's Nest further supports this.

